WEBVTT

1
00:00.000 --> 00:13.488
The Developers page: how agents and code read a Compiled World over MCP and the API.

2
00:13.488 --> 00:17.487
No write tool, and the server refuses to start if one is added.

3
00:17.487 --> 00:22.586
The read-only MCP server is one downloadable file. There is no package to install.

4
00:22.586 --> 00:27.631
The channel manifest lists the version and a hash for every file.

5
00:27.631 --> 00:35.640
Now a terminal. This screen replays a captured session: the commands that ran and the output they printed, unedited.

6
00:35.640 --> 00:44.149
The file is downloaded, hashed, and compared with the manifest value. They match.

7
00:44.149 --> 00:50.651
--version prints the exact build.

8
00:50.651 --> 00:57.155
No TAVONEL variable is set in this shell, so everything below ran without a key.

9
00:57.155 --> 01:04.669
The JSON-RPC requests sent over stdin: initialize, tools/list and one tools/call.

10
01:04.669 --> 01:14.676
The server's responses, exactly as printed.

11
01:14.676 --> 01:22.677
Filtered to names: the tool list. None of them writes.

12
01:22.677 --> 01:29.681
Without a key, the tool call stops at API_KEY_MISSING. This is the real response.

13
01:29.681 --> 01:37.687
--doctor names what is missing and exits with a failure code.

14
01:37.687 --> 01:45.630
The Claude Desktop config block from the MCP docs: the absolute path to the downloaded file, and a placeholder where a key goes.

15
01:45.630 --> 01:50.479
The key lives in the client's env block or its secret facility, never in args.

16
01:50.479 --> 01:54.483
The Claude Desktop app itself is not part of this recording.

17
01:54.483 --> 01:59.831
The docs' tool table, and the note that there is no write tool and no activation tool.

18
01:59.831 --> 02:07.280
A finished Compiled World is open to read in full today. Compiling your own sources is set up with us.
